---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="tokiOS — Distributed Agent Operating System"
  description="tokiOS is an experimental distributed systems architecture for persistent, governed AI agents."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Open technical research</p>

      <h1>Distributed infrastructure for persistent AI agents.</h1>

      <p class="hero-copy">
        tokiOS is an experimental distributed operating architecture for AI agents
        that need persistent state, governed memory, durable execution, and
        auditable behavior across long-running workflows.
      </p>

      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button primary" href="/research/">Explore the research</a>
        <a
          class="button"
          href="/research/tokimind/governed-persistent-memory-300h/"
        >
          Read the tokiMind study
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Research systems</p>
      <h2>A platform for durable agent state.</h2>

      <p class="lead">
        tokiOS separates the broader distributed agent runtime from the systems
        evaluated within it. Current research focuses on governed persistent
        memory and reproducible longitudinal evaluation.
      </p>

      <div class="grid">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>tokiMind</h3>
          <p>
            Governed persistent memory with provenance, authority,
            contradiction handling, supersession, freshness, revocation, and
            scoped retrieval.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>tokiLab</h3>
          <p>
            Experimental infrastructure for frozen, durable, longitudinal
            evaluation of agent behavior and state-management systems.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>tokiOS</h3>
          <p>
            The broader distributed runtime and research platform hosting these
            systems and their future agent-execution architecture.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
